  "text_pages": [
    "Dong-A University Office Of  External International  Affairs > Outbound Programs > Student Exchange Ⅱ\n스킵네비게이션\n본문바로가기\n주메뉴바로가기\nInternational Relations Programs\nDONG-A UNIVERSITY, WHERE WE MAKE YOUR HISTORY\n메인으로 이동\nInternational Relations Programs\nOffice of International Affairs\nAdmission\nGlobal Network\nInternational Relations Programs\nInternational Student Support\nBulletin Boards\n닫기\nOutbound Programs\nOutbound Programs\nIn-Campus Programs\n닫기\nInternational Relations Programs\nInternational Relations Programs\nOutbound Programs\nIn-Campus Programs\nOutbound Programs\nSNS 목록열기\nFACEBOOK 공유하기\nTWITTER 공유하기\nBLOG 공유하기\nSNS 목록닫기\n인쇄\nurl 복사\nStudent Exchange Ⅰ\nStudent Exchange Ⅱ\nDual Degree\nShort Term Language Study\nOverseas Volunteer\nExchange Student (II)\nThis program is the same as the \"Exchange Student Program\" except for the tuition payment portion, and allows students to study language and major at a sister university abroad and earn credits.\nDispatch Conditions\nPeriod of dispatch: Tuition paid by the home school, tuition paid by the partner school\nCredits earned at the counterpart school will be recognized as credits at the home school (credits for majors can be recognized)\nSupport for accommodation placement at the partner school(Depending on the situation of the sister school, dormitories or outside dormitories may be arranged)\nDifferent amounts of support money are provided for different language areas\nEligibility\nUndergraduate students who have completed or are in the process of completing at least two semesters at the University and who are able to study at the University for their final semester.\nLanguage Proficiency\nEnglish-speaking countries : TOEIC score of 750 or above (TOEFL iBT score of 80 or above or IELTS score of 6.5 or above if TOEIC is not accepted by the partner institution)\nJapanese speaking area : JLPT Level 3 (N3) or above, JPT 450 or above (requirements differ depending on the university; if necessary, apply for separate consultation)\nChinese-speaking countries : Holders of the new HSK Level 4 or above or those with equivalent ability\nRecruitment and Dispatch Period\nRecruitment : Once per semester (March, September), with recruitment and selection one semester prior to the semester of dispatch\nDispatch : After recruitment and selection, the following semester (varies by language area)\nUniversities that can be dispatched\n파견 가능 대학 표 정보제공\nCountry\nUniversity name\nDuration\nUnited States\nLander University\nOne semester\nAngelo State University\nOne semester\nSan Francisco State University\nOne semester\nCalifornia State University-Monterey Bay\nOne semester\nJapan\nTeikyo University\nOne semester\nKumamoto University\nOne semester\nRyukoku University\nOne semester\nChina\nDonghua University\nOne semester\nPhilippines\nColegio San Agustin-Bacolod\nOne semester"
  ],
